            <ArticleTitle>Post-dural puncture syndrome in an elderly patient with remote history of previous post-dural puncture syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1049-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>History of previous post-dural puncture syndrome (PDPS) is a strong risk factor for another PDPS when spinal anesthesia is readministered to these patients. We herein report a case to show that this general rule may still apply even after the passage of 50 years.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
